# Written by `ame security virtual-input off` (/usr/libexec/amethystora-hardening), which Steam Input and
# OpenTabletDriver need, and taken away again by `ame security virtual-input on`.
#
# /dev/uinput makes a virtual keyboard or mouse, which types into any window, a root terminal included. The
# image keeps it root's. This gives it to whoever sits at the machine, and so to every app they run that may
# reach all of /dev (Steam, the Chromium browsers, Discord, OBS and Zoom keep --device=all). The node is made
# before the uinput module is loaded, so that nothing waits for it.
## https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/input/uinput.html
## https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/4288
## https://github.com/ValveSoftware/steam-for-linux/issues/4794#issuecomment-327006061

ACTION!="remove", KERNEL=="uinput", SUBSYSTEM=="misc", TAG+="uaccess", OPTIONS+="static_node=uinput"
